### Step 3: Start Customizing Content and Navigation

#### 1. Site Metadata (`_config.yml`)

Set global variables that Jekyll themes display in headers, footers, and page titles:

```yaml
title: Simonas
description: Visual Effects, 3D Post-Production, and Tech Notes
theme: minima

# If your repo is named "hompage" and NOT "username.github.io", set:
baseurl: "/hompage"
url: "https://<your-username>.github.io"

```

#### 2. Add Navigation Pages

Any Markdown file with YAML front matter becomes a page. Create `about.md` in the root folder:

```markdown
---
layout: page
title: About
permalink: /about/
---

## About Me

Write your bio, skills, or portfolio overview here.

```

Themes like `minima` will automatically pick up this page and place a link to `/about/` in the top navigation bar.

